args.newStr:
- Record the exact versions of Python 3.12.x, the JDK (17, 21 or 25; 21 installed), PySpark 4.3.x, the Spark Kafka connector `org.apache.spark:spark-sql-kafka-0-10_2.13:<pyspark version>` (explain it is resolved at runtime through `spark.jars.packages` in the session builder, which needs network access on first use, or can be shipped as a jar), the Kafka client library, the Kafka image and all pinned dependencies, taken from task 1.1. Note the Windows `HADOOP_HOME`/`winutils` requirement if needed.
- Provide copy-pasteable PowerShell commands that work from a fresh clone, all through the venv interpreter:
  - check `java -version`;
  - create the venv (`py -3.12 -m venv .venv`) and check `python --version` prints 3.12.x;
  - install (`.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt`);
  - run tests (`.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest`);
  - state that the CLIs and test fixture set `PYSPARK_PYTHON` and `PYSPARK_DRIVER_PYTHON` to the venv python;
